   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1fe3316d-2fc0-4082-b16d-a76694ea9c21",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.3 Flatten the scan dimensions\n",
    "(220, 220, 66, 66) → (48400, 66, 66). The result is a view, so it uses no extra memory, and `measurements_list` stays 4D for the cells above."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "89f3f35a-eda2-48b9-a27c-703e48a5cdc4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "torch.Size([48400, 66, 66])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "measurements_flat = []\n",
    "for mi in measurements_list:\n",
    "    ms = mi.shape\n",
    "    measurements_flat.append(th.as_tensor(mi).view(ms[0] * ms[1], ms[2], ms[3]))\n",
    "print(measurements_flat[0].shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6cefc0dc-478e-4e4c-a3e6-b501a52ea516",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Build the model\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.1 Volume and multislice geometry\n",
    "The potential volume starts as zeros (296³, complex). The beam direction is split into 8 slices, so each slice is `bin_factor` voxels thick. The beam energy is 80 keV."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "f1f83f44-c7fa-4e10-9e83-f8857b741c01",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "bin_factor: 296   slice_thickness: 117.27127440327973\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "V_shape = (V_shape1D, V_shape1D, V_shape1D)\n",
    "V_model = th.zeros(V_shape, dtype=th.complex64).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "slice_number = 1\n",
    "bin_factor = V_shape1D // slice_number\n",
    "slice_thickness = bin_factor * dx\n",
    "print('bin_factor:', bin_factor, '  slice_thickness:', slice_thickness)\n",
    "\n",
    "E = 80e3                 # beam energy (eV)\n",
    "lam = wavelength(E)\n",
    "dx_xy = [dx, dx]         # pixel size along both axes, for the propagator\n",
    "shape = (M1, M1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "94d57f05-f672-479f-b69d-b8ea5d17b326",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Nmodes: 3\n",
      "B:      1\n",
      "N:      tensor([296, 296], dtype=torch.int32)\n",
      "M:      tensor([66, 66], dtype=torch.int32)\n",
      "K:      48400\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Problem sizes\n",
    "Nmodes = probes_scaled[0].shape[0]                 # probe modes\n",
    "B = 1\n",
    "N = th.tensor([V_shape[0], V_shape[2]]).int()     # volume lateral size\n",
    "M = th.tensor([M1, M1]).int()                     # probe window size\n",
    "K = positions_list[0].shape[0]                    # scan positions per tilt\n",
    "print('Nmodes:', Nmodes)\n",
    "print('B:     ', B)\n",
    "print('N:     ', N)\n",
    "print('M:     ', M)\n",
    "print('K:     ', K)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "786f4ade-1f0f-452a-98bd-23eb9b75e87b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2 PSF kernel for the binning regularisation\n",
    "A smoothing kernel built with `regularize_multilayers` and cropped around its centre. The model uses it to regularise the effect of binning voxels into slices."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "64ed72c2-9370-4b29-ba8d-683f9732c75e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "2.14.1+cu126 ['sm_50', 'sm_60', 'sm_70', 'sm_75', 'sm_80', 'sm_86', 'sm_90']\n",
      "tensor([2., 2., 2.], device='cuda:0')\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import torch as th\n",
    "print(th.__version__, th.cuda.get_arch_list())\n",
    "print(th.ones(3, device='cuda:0') * 2)   # a real GPU operation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "8a790e7a-956e-4489-b484-1e15e9ca71b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "kernel shape: torch.Size([1, 5, 73, 5])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "kernel_num = 297\n",
    "psf_shape = 297\n",
    "kernel_shape = [kernel_num, kernel_num, kernel_num]\n",
    "psf = np.zeros([psf_shape, psf_shape, psf_shape])\n",
    "psf[0, 0, 0] = 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Wa = regularize_multilayers(kernel_shape, 90, alpha=1)\n",
    "psf2 = np.fft.ifftn(np.fft.fftn(psf) * Wa).real\n",
    "\n",
    "m0, m1, m2 = 146, 112, 146\n",
    "psf3 = fftshift(psf2)[m2:-m2, m0:-m0, m1:-m1]\n",
    "psfimg = fftshift(psf2[0])[m0:-m0, m1:-m1]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "im = ax.imshow(psfimg)\n",
    "plt.colorbar(im)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "kernel = th.as_tensor(np.swapaxes(psf3, 1, 2)).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n",
    "print('kernel shape:', kernel.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "daa51bd6-5e6b-4c47-9d3b-e33cb2d02751",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.3 Move inputs to the GPU\n",
    "Angles, translations, positions, probes and the Fresnel propagator."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "f8997dc3-5d41-4c9f-9d79-8cc078f9f38d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n_angles = len(phi)\n",
    "angles = th.zeros((3, n_angles), device=device)\n",
    "angles[0, :] = th.as_tensor(phi).to(device)\n",
    "angles[1, :] = th.as_tensor(theta).to(device)\n",
    "angles[2, :] = th.as_tensor(psi).to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "start_end = [[[0, V_shape[0]], [0, V_shape[2]]]] * n_angles\n",
    "translations = [th.tensor([[ti[0]], [ti[1]]], device=device) for ti in translation]\n",
    "positions = [th.as_tensor(posi).to(device) for posi in positions_list]\n",
    "dr = dr_list\n",
    "error_norm = error_norm_list\n",
    "probe_model = [[th.as_tensor(p).unsqueeze(1).to(device).requires_grad_(False)]\n",
    "               for p in probes_scaled]\n",
    "propagator = Propagator(slice_thickness, lam, dx_xy, shape, device=device)\n",
    "\n",
    "error_norm_total = th.sum(th.stack(error_norm)).clone().cpu().numpy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "21171b26-3fb9-47bd-9808-29c7ba5cc41c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.4 Create the model\n",
    "`tau1`, `tau2` are model hyper-parameters, and `braggpix` / `butterorder` set the Butterworth filter. If you rebuild the model after a run, re-run 4.1 first so the volume starts from zeros again."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 24,
   "id": "f7fac988-db69-4d4f-80fc-146ee6a5ee17",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tau1 = 1e-9\n",
    "tau2 = 3e-9\n",
    "braggpix = 113\n",
    "butterorder = 5\n",
    "\n",
    "model = MultiSlicePtychographyTomographyModel(V_model,\n",
    "                                              probe_model,\n",
    "                                              positions,\n",
    "                                              dr,\n",
    "                                              error_norm,\n",
    "                                              angles=angles,\n",
    "                                              tau1=tau1,\n",
    "                                              tau2=tau2,\n",
    "                                              translations=translations,\n",
    "                                              start_end_model=start_end,\n",
    "                                              loss_function=amplitude_loss,\n",
    "                                              propagator=propagator,\n",
    "                                              braggpix=braggpix,\n",
    "                                              butterorder=butterorder,\n",
    "                                              dx=dx,\n",
    "                                              bin_factor=bin_factor,\n",
    "                                              intensity_scaling_factor=1,\n",
    "                                              kernel=kernel,\n",
    "                                              subpix_shift=False)"
   ]
  },
